 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-nagata-rees-algebra",
  "def-nagata-rees-piece"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By [def-nagata-affine-blowup], the affine blow-up is\n$\\operatorname{Proj}(\\mathcal R_A(I))\\to\\operatorname{Spec}A$, the\nstructural morphism of Proj followed by the isomorphism\n$\\operatorname{Spec}\\mathcal R_A(I)_0\\cong\\operatorname{Spec}A$ induced by\n$\\mathcal R_A(I)_0\\cong A$ ([lemma-nagata-rees-degree-zero]), with the grading of [prop-nagata-rees-graded].\nSince $I$ is finitely generated, the Rees algebra is of finite type over\nits degree-zero part ([prop-nagata-rees-finite-generation]). The\nverified properness instance for $\\operatorname{Proj}$ of a graded ring of\nfinite type over its degree-zero part ([def-nagata-affine-proj]) makes the\nstructural morphism proper, and composing with an isomorphism keeps it\nproper.",
   "uses": [
    "def-nagata-affine-blowup",
    "lemma-nagata-rees-degree-zero",
    "prop-nagata-rees-graded",
    "prop-nagata-rees-finite-generation",
    "def-nagata-affine-proj"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
